  "canonical_machine_sources": {
    "comm-create-lazy-claude-codex-skills/SKILL.md": {
      "source_path": "harness/common/skills/comm-create-lazy-claude-codex-skills/SKILL.md",
      "sha256": "909a097a37781b329068ca281eb0c1ef24e235150272584d132745adbc43670c",
      "utf8_text": "---\nname: comm-create-lazy-claude-codex-skills\ndescription: Use when designing, creating or substantially editing working Codex and Claude skills or rules.\n---\n\n# Author one instruction\n\nUse using-superpowers before authoring. Establish task, useful result, intended\nharness and destination; cwd is not proof. Before design/substantial edits read\n[content and form selection](references/content-contract.md).\n\n1. Inspect existing owners/rules/resources/checks. Covered → reuse; a small gap\n   → amend its owner. Select by independent result, not theme or old name.\n2. Compare rule-only, lazy-skill-only and rule+skill before choosing. Record why\n   each form fits or fails, then select the minimum sufficient form; default\n   contextual procedures to lazy skills. A rule needs a concrete pre-selection\n   failure that lazy metadata cannot prevent.\n3. Produce inputs → actions → result → observable completion, with limits,\n   approvals/stops/missing data and exact tested conditions for resource reading.\n4. Before writing follow the authorized inbox route from root\n   `harness/common/skills/comm-process-harness-inbox/SKILL.md`; keep a full dated\n   candidate and permanent rationale/evidence outside working instructions.\n\nDone: justified form and compact complete candidate preserving every contract\nand both-mode dependencies. Design alone is not validation or publication.\nWhen checking is requested use\n`harness/common/skills/comm-validate-harness-instructions/SKILL.md`;\nwhen publishing use\n`harness/common/skills/comm-publish-harness-instructions/SKILL.md`.\nDo not load these stages for an unrelated request. Protected entrypoints and\ncanonical priority remain mandatory.\n"
    },
    "comm-create-lazy-claude-codex-skills/references/content-contract.md": {
      "source_path": "harness/common/skills/comm-create-lazy-claude-codex-skills/references/content-contract.md",
      "sha256": "8ce61cf6e8f183d6e5e5f5e19a74346f9edfde1caa963588602d574bd1414f80",
      "utf8_text": "# Content and form\n\nEach new/substantial edit: name behavior, trigger and observable result;\ninspect existing skills/rules/resources/tests. Covered → reuse without a new\nrecord; a narrow gap → amend its owner. Own request/result/independent check\n→ consider a separate owner; one result's detail → conditional resource.\nTheme/old name is not ownership; no skill-count quota.\n\n## Select before authoring\n\nCompare all three forms against the actual need:\n\n| Form | Sufficient when |\n| --- | --- |\n| Rule only | A short boundary must apply before procedure selection; no separate algorithm is needed. |\n| Context-dependent lazy skill only | A recognizable task needs a procedure; name/description can trigger its loading. Default for contextual procedures. |\n| Rule + lazy skill | A concrete failure must be prevented before skill selection, lazy metadata is insufficient, and the detailed procedure belongs only in matching tasks. |\n\nFor a rule, name the pre-selection failure and explain why lazy discovery cannot\nprevent it. Brevity, habit and \"more reliable\" alone are not evidence. A discovery\nmiss first calls for improving name/description and checking loading; it does\nnot automatically justify a rule. Preserve existing mandatory boundaries.\n\nWeigh persistent context cost, discovery, procedural cohesion and drift. Choose\nthe minimum sufficient form, including reuse/no change. Briefly record why each\nof the three forms fits or fails, including rejected alternatives, and the choice\nin the authorized request or permanent rationale,\noutside working instructions. Make technical choices within existing authority;\nthis adds no universal user approval gate.\n\nIn a pair, the rule owns the necessary early boundary and the skill owns the\nalgorithm. Duplicating a critical boundary needs specific justification; a\nmandatory algorithm alone does not justify an always-loaded rule.\n\nWhen validation is authorized, test form choice and discovery behavior:\nlazy-only, rule-only, justified pair, reuse/amendment, metadata repair and\nunrelated non-loading. Use real behavior, explicit/implicit discovery and\nboth-mode checks under the existing validation owner. Missing checks remain\nunverified; drafting the rationale is not proof of discovery.\n\n## Preserve the content contract\n\nWrite inputs → actions → result → observable completion, when-read pointers,\nmissing data/approvals/stops/limits. Headings optional; metadata selects.\nRemove repeats/advice/history; examples prevent mistakes.\nRationale/evidence permanent outside instructions/inbox. Preserve obligations/\nboth-mode dependencies with tested pointers, no mandatory chain of all skills.\n\nGoals: SKILL usually ≤200 words; resource sum ≤1000 static tokens,\nresolve >1200 deferred; evaluate-skill A/no errors. No raised thresholds,\nhidden resources or fake manifests/coverage.\n\nProfile: nonempty YAML name/description; name 1–64 [a-z0-9-], no edge hyphen/--,\nfolder match, shared comm-/proj-; description 1–1024 chars, trigger/capability.\nSKILL alone suffices; references/scripts/assets optional guidance/actions/outputs;\nagents/openai.yaml UI/policy/deps. Exclude human bodies.\nRules scope/behavior in body, no paths metadata; Claude ignores metadata\nexcept paths. Verify Codex loading separately.\n"
    },
    "comm-validate-harness-instructions/SKILL.md": {
      "source_path": "harness/common/skills/comm-validate-harness-instructions/SKILL.md",
      "sha256": "3e306fd9dc37363b12c008a730ed12c4bbc14b16dccc07f6f5874d7c48e0fdf8",
      "utf8_text": "---\nname: comm-validate-harness-instructions\ndescription: Use when checking an existing harness instruction or candidate, interpreting findings, or establishing its verification status without publication.\n---\n\n# Validate the current version\n\nIdentify version, target kind, contract, modes, available tools and authorized\nchecks. Before tests read [validation](references/validation.md); before plugin-eval\nread [evaluation](references/evaluation.md). For content/profile checks read from\nroot `harness/common/skills/comm-create-lazy-claude-codex-skills/references/content-contract.md`.\n\n1. Run applicable mandatory checks on the final compact version; separate\n   structural, budget, code and native behavior findings. Missing tools/checks\n   remain unverified; warn and offer authorized installation.\n2. Repair confirmed causes only when authorized, then repeat ALL current\n   mandatory checks. Never inflate drafts, thresholds or coverage to get A.\n3. Record startup+metadata, comparable actual reads with ALL dependencies and\n   full available resources separately, with baseline paths/versions/limits.\n4. Report date/version/files/commands/tools/agent versions/scope/contract,\n   compactness/actual thresholds/baseline differences/excess reasons,\n   pass/fail/not-run/N/A+reason, findings/missing tools/next steps and statuses\n   separately for each agent/mode.\n\nDone: truthful current results with no unresolved correctness/discovery/behavior\n gaps for verified scope. Edits reset statuses. This does not publish; copying\nor permission never upgrades status. Saving results follows the authorized\ninbox/evidence route.\n"
    },
    "comm-validate-harness-instructions/references/evaluation.md": {
      "source_path": "harness/common/skills/comm-validate-harness-instructions/references/evaluation.md",
      "sha256": "7203060c251d479529172a42dd913a9c607b0b79a44ecb69aec555e583eba33d",
      "utf8_text": "# Evaluation\n\nRequires Node + a trusted ordinary installed plugin-eval JS entry in entry.\nDo not pass a symlink or resolve a shell shim to bypass rejection; verify the\nchosen original entry and ancestors before use. Set skill_dir to selected root:\n\n```sh\nnode harness/common/scripts/plugin_eval_without_human.mjs \"$entry\" start \"$skill_dir\" --format json\n```\n\nThen analyze. Own skill folder or bounded generic directory for\nplain instructions, not single Markdown. Structural/budget/code findings,\nJSON improvementBrief/compare. Save stdout outside target; no --output,\n--brief-out/benchmark writes or external metric-packs. README.human.md filter rejects nested/alias reads before content/cost;\nsources/tool unchanged. Avoid author-home/cache paths.\nPromises API, not OS isolation or protection against concurrent path substitution.\nThe launcher rejects symlink inputs/ancestors and the whole working harness tree;\ninterpreter and installed analyzer code remain trusted execution dependencies. After updates rerun via .venv Python pytest:\nharness/common/testing/tests/test_plugin_eval_without_human.py.\n"
    },
    "comm-validate-harness-instructions/references/validation.md": {
      "source_path": "harness/common/skills/comm-validate-harness-instructions/references/validation.md",
      "sha256": "0f9c37a876a4b36d2ed8d4bcdc0d3185e0b314eba3db6b3bcbd84bae76ac4949",
      "utf8_text": "# Checks and behavior\n\nSave contract/scenarios: applicability/actions/completion, limits, permissions,\nstops and missing data. RED without new guidance → compact candidate → GREEN;\nrepeat ALL mandatory checks after edits/before publication. Do not create an\nartificial long draft to show shrinkage or artificially shrink compact material.\nApplicable skill-creator/external checks are mandatory in every project.\n\nHelpers: using-superpowers; skill-creator design/final quick_validate;\nwriting-skills behavioral RED–GREEN–REFACTOR; plugin-eval start→analyze;\nimprove-skill JSON brief→required/recommended fixes→re-evaluate/compare;\nopenai-docs official sources; plugin-management integration/install.\nEvaluate-plugin requires real manifest; plain rules use content/conflicts/\nresources/compactness, not skill-only validation. Generic analysis is not\nskill/plugin/native proof; installed tool is not verified behavior.\nMissing tools → warn, offer authorized install, unverified. Benchmark/config/\ndependency writes require authorization; Python dependencies use uv.\n\nEach final version: Codex and Claude separately, common-only neutral project\nand combined preserving existing project, native listing, explicit own-resource\ninvocation, implicit choice, unrelated non-loading and actual behavior.\nCheck rule reading, loader human exclusion and behavior separately; instructions\ndo not technically block file access. Installation/template checks read from root\n`harness/common/skills/comm-install-harness/SKILL.md`; project-only refuses,\nnever infer a shared skeleton. For suite/configuration read only as needed\n`harness/common/skills/comm-install-harness/references/testing.md`.\n\nMeasure baseline/current startup guards+metadata, comparable actual task reads\nwith complete dependencies, and total available resources separately. Record\npaths/versions/factual thresholds/differences/growth/excess reasons/next steps.\nStatic tokens are not usage/cost; no agreed startup cap. Required resource\nremains in its assessed owner; tested when-read pointers and both-mode access.\nReport real status/scope; verified needs all mandatory current checks and no\ncorrectness/discovery/behavior gaps. Evidence belongs in testing/evidence,\nnot checks; retain rationale/results independently of inbox.\n"
    }
  },
